---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Tiktoken } from 'js-tiktoken/lite';
import gpt2 from 'js-tiktoken/ranks/gpt2';
import cl100k from 'js-tiktoken/ranks/cl100k_base';
import o200k from 'js-tiktoken/ranks/o200k_base';

// My name through three generations of OpenAI tokenizers, counted at build time.
const encoders = [new Tiktoken(gpt2), new Tiktoken(cl100k), new Tiktoken(o200k)];
const counts = (s: string) => encoders.map((e) => e.encode(s).length);
const english = counts('Deepak Nelapatla');
const telugu = counts('దీపక్ నేలపాటి');
const cheaper = Math.floor(telugu[0] / telugu[2]);
---
<Base title="about">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I’m Deepak Nelapatla, a machine learning engineer on the ML4H team at the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard.</p>
    <p>Most of my work is with longitudinal EHR notes: years of clinical text written about a patient over time. Right now I’m building models that use those notes to predict disease, focusing on late-life depression and stroke.</p>

    <h2 id="model-card">Model card</h2>
    <dl class="post-facts model-card">
      <div><dt>Model</dt><dd>deepak-24</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Pretraining</dt><dd>B.Tech, Electronics and Communication Engineering · JNTU Hyderabad</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Fine-tuning</dt><dd>M.S., Computer Science (AI/ML) · UT Arlington</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Deployed</dt><dd>ML4H · Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Eval</dt><dd><a href="/posts/benchmarks-picked-the-wrong-winner">the leaderboard picked the wrong winner</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Intended use</dt><dd>reading clinical notes; writing these ones</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Known issues</dt><dd>always up for a game</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="name-tokens">My name, tokenized by GPT-2 → GPT-4 → GPT-4o: <span lang="en">Deepak Nelapatla</span> is {english.join(' → ')} tokens. In Telugu, <span lang="te">దీపక్ నేలపాటి</span> is {telugu.join(' → ')}. It got {cheaper}× cheaper to say my name.</p>

    <h2>Why “tokenizer”</h2>
    <p>Before a language model can read anything, a tokenizer breaks the text into small pieces. That’s what this site is for me: breaking work, life and play into pieces small enough to think about. On the homepage, a small model reads my system prompt and tries to predict what I’ll say, one token at a time. Where it guesses wrong, that’s me.</p>

    <h2>How notes grow</h2>
    <p>Most of these notes start with a pen in a paper notebook. Each one is marked with a stage:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Seedling</strong>: a rough idea, barely formed.</li>
      <li><strong>Budding</strong>: taking shape, still being revised.</li>
      <li><strong>Evergreen</strong>: finished enough to stand on its own.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <dl class="post-facts">
      <div><dt>Tokenizer</dt><dd>o200k_base (GPT-4o) via js-tiktoken, counted at build</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Funnel Display, Geist, Geist Mono</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Decode</dt><dd>Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, teacher-forced offline on my own words</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Built with</dt><dd>Astro, a few small inline scripts, no framework</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hosted on</dt><dd>Vercel</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <h2>Say hi</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:nelapatladeepak@gmail.com">nelapatladeepak@gmail.com</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
